  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Marie Stopes International Yemen - Family Planning and Re-productive Health (IV)</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project will focus on reaching underserved women and youth with quality and accessible FP and SRH services through expanding service provision where there is a lack of public services and a high unmet need. MSIY will deliver services through different channels (e.g. clinics, franchised midwives, call lines) in order to respond flexibly to the rapidly changing needs. MSIY will introduce the provision of quality BEmONC services, strengthen and expand the support provided to MSIY&#x2019;s Social Franchise network of midwives and public sector support providers, and maintain quality service delivery of FP and post-miscarriage care services across its channels. MSIY has the staff, technical capacity and institutional resources needed to deliver this much needed increase in access to SRHR in Yemen.</narrative>
  </description>
